From 5b18fb3204f6a10de99f5237a74bead23a0184f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jack Walters <jackwalterswork@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:38:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] git_ui: Place review comments on the merge request's own
 diff before posting

GitLab takes a comment only on a line of its diff between base_sha and
head_sha, while the view shows the file on disk, which can be ahead of,
behind, or edited since head_sha. Posting a line GitLab could not find
failed with an opaque 400 about a blank line code. Each comment's line is
now mapped onto head_sha through git, looked up in the merge request's
diff to learn whether it is added or unchanged, and given a real line
code; a comment that cannot be placed is reported by path and line with
the reason, and the rest still post.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
